                      v4.7
                            
This file provides a detailed description of how to build and install the 
TRANSM code.

The TRANSM code currently only has only serial running capability. The only 
prerequisite for building the TRANSM is a (modern) C++ compiler, such as 
g++. The TRANSM code, requires the following external libraries:

  - BOOST (A set of additional C++ libraries in addition to STL)
    https://www.boost.org/
    
  - Google Performance Tools (A collection of a high-performance multi-threaded 
    memory allocations implementation)
    https://goog-perftools.sourceforge.net/
  
  - SQLite (A C-language library that implements an efficient SQL database engine)
    https://www.sqlite.org/index.html

  - GoogleTest (Google Test is a unit testing library for the C++ programming language
    https://github.com/google/googletest)

Other external libraries are installed with the TRANSM:

  - CPEAC v4.4a (A Monte Carlo simulation model of the progression and outcomes of 
    HIV disease)
    TRANSM repo: https://github.com/hsphcdm/cepac
    Original: https://www.massgeneral.org/medicine/mpec/research/cpac-model
  
  - tclap (A simple C++ library that facilitates parsing command line)
    Forked in TRANSM repo: https://github.com/hsphcdm/tclap
    
  - pugixml (A C++ XML processing library)
    Forked in TRANSM repo: https://github.com/hsphcdm/pugixml

Quick Start with TRANSM
=======================
Build in MacOS and Linux Ubuntu:
    ./build.sh
   

Build with Spack Libraries (Recommended)
========================================
To build the code using Spack package manager one should first install the Spack with:

    git clone -c feature.manyFiles=true https://github.com/spack/spack.git

To setup Spack run . share/spack/setup-env.sh. This will modify your environment and put 
Spack in your path.  If you want to have spack always on you will need to update your 
.bashrc with source <PATHTOSPACK>/share/spack/setup-env.sh

then install the following packages using %gcc@8.5.0 

    gperftools, boost, googletest, sqlite, cmake
    
with the following command as an example:

    spack install boost@1.82.0 %gcc@8.5.0

then adding the following line to .bashrc

    spack load gperftools
    spack load boost@1.82.0
    spack load googltest
    spack load python
    spack load sqlite
    spack load cmake

Then simply run the build command:
  
    ./build.sh 

To avoid conflic with the local BOOST library DBOOST_ROOT=<path/to/boost>. Where <path/to/boost> can be found via:

    spack location -i boost

Build in FASRC (Not available anymore)
======================================
To build the code at Harvard University Faculty of Arts and Sciences Research Computing 
(a.k.a FASRC) a password and verification code (not the same as Harvard Key) are required 
to log in to FASRC. For example, ssh to the cluster can be done by:

    ssh -X sseifi@login.rc.fas.harvard.edu

The modules to build and run TRANSM requires the following versions listed below:

    module load gcc/9.3.0-fasrc01
    module load cmake/3.5.2-fasrc01
    module load boost/1.63.0-fasrc01
    module load gperftools
    module load sqlite/3081101-fasrc01

For linking the loaded Boost library to the compiler, the path the loaded boost library 
has to be defined:

    export BOOST_DIR=/n/helmod/apps/centos7/Core/boost/1.63.0-fasrc01/
    export BOOST_LIBRARYDIR=/n/helmod/apps/centos7/Core/boost/1.72.0-fasrc01/lib

Then simply run the build command:
  
    ./build.sh
